k cards. If we play and force the landlord to pass or be beaten, teammate gets turn — good chance to shed cards.\n\nLandlord played early strong combo — maybe trying to dominate. We should challenge that momentum.\n\nBest move: **888 + JJ** — minimal sufficient strength.\n\nReason: Playing ♠8 ♥8 ♣8 ♠J ♣J (triplet 8s with pair Js) is the weakest winning move, conserving higher cards for future plays while disrupting the landlord\'s control. It uses redundant mid-level cards efficiently and gives our teammate a chance to act with potentially supportive follow-up options.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠8", "♥8", "♣8", "♠J", "♣J"]}'}
